      "id": "xklta11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Rise of New Religions"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Vardhamana Mahavira was the 24th Tirthankara who organized Jain teachings, emphasizing extreme asceticism and absolute non-violence (Ahimsa).",
        "Jainism teaches the Three Jewels (Triratna): Right Faith, Right Knowledge, and Right Conduct.",
        "Gautama Buddha established Buddhism after attaining Enlightenment at Bodh Gaya, proposing the Middle Path (Madhyam Marga).",
        "Buddhism revolves around the Four Noble Truths and the Eightfold Path (Ashtangika Marga) to achieve Nirvana.",
        "Buddhist canonical literature is collected in the Three Tripitakas: Vinaya Pitaka, Sutta Pitaka, and Abhidhamma Pitaka."
      ],
      "id": "lmdxjix"
    },
